 "produced_at_commit": "67a5678",
 "producer": "claude-opus-5[1m] in an isolated worktree on branch warp-0717-subset-runner",
 "question": "Does running `shared + the measured transitive prerequisite closure of a fragment` reproduce EXACTLY the labels that fragment produces in the full run, and how long does it take, against the prefix that --upto already runs?",
 "method": [
  "region-level prerequisite closures are READ from proof/WARP-0712/order-dependence.json (key `closures`, digest e8b70e982e750436c6e65e7874b5df7c8ed5cebd085ea68cfe9acbe109cdfa9d), not re-measured: producing them runs the suite once per region and is minutes.",
  "region -> fragment from each fragment's declared region range in scripts/suites/manifest.json.",
  "DIRECT demand of fragment F = the fragments owning the regions F's own regions were measured to need. TRANSITIVE closure = the fixpoint of that relation. The direct demand ALONE was measured INSUFFICIENT: see direct_demand_insufficient below.",
  "one FULL run recording every assertion label tagged with the emitting fragment, by wrapping shared.expect; then one fresh process per fragment running shared + closure(F) in manifest order, recording the labels F emitted.",
  "comparison is F's label MULTISET plus each label's pass/fail outcome, full versus closure.",
  "per-fragment wall time is measured in ONE full run with a monotonic clock around each fragment's exec, so it is the real cost of the real run and not a per-fragment subprocess. closure_measured_s is the measured wall time of the closure run including shared.",
  "WHICH FIGURES ARE MEASURED AND WHICH ARE MODELLED, corrected for review 1's C7. MEASURED: own_fragment_s (a monotonic clock around each fragment's exec inside one full run), closure_measured_s (the wall time of that fragment's closure run), and own_labels_full_run / own_labels_closure_run. MODELLED: prefix_modelled_s and closure_modelled_s, which are SUMS of the per-fragment measured times for the prefix and for the closure, plus shared, and NOT runs of `--upto` or `--suite`. saved_vs_prefix_s is the difference of two modelled numbers. Nothing here timed a shipped command: the artifact that does is proof/WARP-0717/timings.txt, and review 1's independent runs of the shipped commands landed within about 2 percent of these models. The MODELLED figures are what the AC1 amendment's `against the prefix` numbers come from, and it now says so."
 ],
 "direct_demand_insufficient": {
  "outcome": "the DIRECT demand is NOT closed under its own relation and was measured to fail",
  "measured": "with direct demand only, 8 of 13 fragments were CLOSED and 5 of 13 produced ZERO of their own labels because a fragment INSIDE the closure crashed first",
  "witness": "13_warp_0623_codified_live's direct demand names 06_capabilities_manifest_honesty_warp but not 03 or 04, which 06's own demand names; the run died on NameError: name '_FakeLoop' is not defined inside 06, before 13 began",
  "fragments_that_failed_on_direct_demand_only": [
